WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.555
Glitch Hunt is a full stack AI playtesting platform.

00:00:02.555 --> 00:00:07.713
An agent explores a puzzle game, applies the same inputs to two builds, and produces replayable evidence.

00:00:07.713 --> 00:00:11.496
This edited tour uses actual application recordings with synthetic narration.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.436
Each published run has a read only link showing its outcome, model calls, estimated cost, and completed replay.

00:00:20.436 --> 00:00:22.052
An operator can revoke that link.

00:00:22.052 --> 00:00:25.921
Launching paid work and changing sharing settings still require authentication.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.744
The activity trace separates decisions from execution.

00:00:32.744 --> 00:00:34.523
The model chooses a named landmark.

00:00:34.523 --> 00:00:40.520
A deterministic navigator applies individual moves, while an independent search verifies completion and route budgets.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:44.280
Observations, request latency, scheduled waiting, and tokens stay visible.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.220
The batch API stores jobs in PostgreSQL before queue dispatch.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:52.480
Private Vercel consumers claim leases, follow shared limits, and save checkpoints.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.869
Repair dispatch can republish unfinished jobs.

00:00:54.869 --> 00:00:58.661
Lease fencing prevents an expired worker from overwriting a newer result.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.476
Early hosted experiments left many trials unfinished.

00:01:02.476 --> 00:01:05.980
Checkpoint recovery, clearer tools, and request pacing improved completion.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:09.298
The comparison preserves earlier reports and their different deadlines.

00:01:09.298 --> 00:01:14.110
Since several settings changed together, these results document progress rather than isolate one cause.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.395
The recovery drill terminates an actual worker after two saved moves.

00:01:18.395 --> 00:01:22.478
A replacement resumes and completes the level using three real model calls overall.

00:01:22.478 --> 00:01:24.200
Duplicate delivery adds no attempt.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.053
Cancellation blocks further checkpoints and stale results.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.775
The database is local and isolated.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.882
Key Management adds persistent inventory to the game state.

00:01:32.882 --> 00:01:37.279
The agent collects a key, crosses a locked door, reaches the pressure plate, and finishes.

00:01:37.279 --> 00:01:39.234
A broken key pickup prevents completion.

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:43.191
The current catalogue contains thirty six labelled level and update combinations.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.090
The hosted benchmark completed all sixty trials at one, five, and twenty worker slots.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:53.560
It verified forty five regressions and fifteen healthy cases with zero misses or false alarms.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.652
The shared provider quota limits throughput.

00:01:55.652 --> 00:01:58.600
Explore the public replays and source to inspect the evidence.
